.TH KIRO-PARU-AUR-CHECK 8 "2026-11-26" "Kiro" "Kiro System Tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-paru-aur-check \- switch the AUR check before paru builds on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-paru-aur-check
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-\-enable\fR | \fB\-\-disable\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-paru-aur-check
manages one line in
.IR /etc/paru.conf ,
under
.BR [bin] :
.PP
.EX
# Kiro: AUR check \(em shows risky PKGBUILD lines before paru builds (kiro-aur-check)
PreBuildCommand = /usr/local/bin/kiro-aur-check
.EE
.PP
Without an option it adds that line only when there is no Kiro marker and no
PreBuildCommand yet. A pacman hook runs it that way whenever paru or kiro-system-files is
installed or updated, so the check is on by default, and a choice someone made (the check
switched off, or a PreBuildCommand of their own) is never overwritten.
.PP
paru reads only one config file. Someone with their own
.I ~/.config/paru/paru.conf
needs the line there as well.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-enable
Switch the check on (refused when paru.conf already runs another PreBuildCommand).
.TP
.B \-\-disable
Switch it off: the line is commented out, the marker stays.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print on, off, other (another PreBuildCommand) or no-paru. Needs no root.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/paru.conf
paru's system config (owned by the paru package).
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.d/hooks/kiro-paru-aur-check.hook
Runs this command after paru or kiro-system-files changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kiro-aur-check (8),
.BR paru.conf (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Dubois <https://www.erikdubois.be>
